  "hypothesis": "H2 (embedding structure): the token embedding W_E over integers 0..112 is sparse in the Fourier basis mod 113 \u2014 a handful of key frequencies carry most of the norm. Against: Fourier power spread roughly evenly across all 56 frequencies (no frequency with >>1/56 share).",
  "result": "E0003 (local-full): W_E Fourier power is sparse. Top frequencies 28 (28.5%), 17 (23.1%), 2 (20.0%), 14 (7.2%); uniform share would be 1.8%. 9 key freqs hold 91.8% of power. Saved subspace A0001 (dim 18).",
  "revised_example": {
   "text": "E0006 (local-full, full grid, mean ablation): each head alone removes 28-34% of the logit diff (0.1: 72.4->47.9; 0.0: ->50.3; 0.2: ->51.2; 0.3: ->52.0). All 4 matter about equally, but none is needed on its own: the logit diff stays ~50, which is still a big margin. Revised: the heads share the work (each carries part of the frequency set?). Still to test: mlp0 alone, and all heads together.",
